    "label": "SbmA alterations reduce PR-39 susceptibility",
    "mechanism_type": "OTHER",
    "note": "Salmonella enterica serovar Typhimurium mutants with SbmA alterations were about fourfold less susceptible and showed slower killing without an obvious measured fitness cost. The study called SbmA a putative transport protein but did not directly measure uptake, so the specific resistance route remains unresolved."
  },
